From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] client: less loading when windows open and turns start

Profiled on the ODROID-GO Advance (Cortex-A35): the stops of a third to
half a second when a window opened or a turn started were loading, not
drawing.

- Every sound played was read and converted again (resampled from 22 to
  44 kHz), the cached ones too, the uncached ones twice: playSoundImpl
  loaded it before it looked at the cache. At the start of a turn the
  new day's sound and the map's ambient sounds took ~200 ms.
- Every animation copied its file's layout, twice, and a portrait file
  lists all creatures (the info bar's garrison, the kingdom overview's
  heroes). The layout is now shared with RenderHandler's cache and
  copied only when an animation changes it (flips, added frames).
  Registering icons copies a shared cached layout instead of changing
  it, so animations keep the layout they were made with, as before.
- Images are cached only while something uses them: closing a window let
  go of its images, and opening it again read and decoded them again
  (mods' PNG files). When bare_app runs the client (0001) the images
  used last stay loaded, up to 64 MB counted as 32-bit pixels.
- The new game list read the headers of all the maps whenever it opened
  (226 maps here: about a second). When bare_app runs the client they
  are read once a session, in the background while the main menu is up;
  the list waits for that read if it opens before it ends.
- SDL converts a sound's rate with a windowed sinc filter: ~0.1 s for a
  few seconds of a 22 kHz sound, and sounds load as they are first
  played (a battle's start, every new creature). When bare_app runs the
  client, WAV files (8 or 16 bits, mono or stereo) are converted to the
  device's format by linear interpolation; anything else goes to SDL.

The kingdom overview opened again: 330 ms -> 90 ms. The start of a turn
stopped the game for 360-460 ms, now 50-160 ms; the first battle of a
game 515 ms -> ~400 ms; opening the new game list 2.1 s -> 0.96 s, again
~0.5 s.

Upstream: not submitted (only keeping images is specific to the SDK)
Signed-off-by: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
